<section class="inner-sec">
  <div class="sec-eyebrow">How it works on the floor</div>
  <h2>Every call answered, every chair rebooked</h2>
  <p class="lede">One receptionist covers the phone, the texts, the website and the socials — answering what's routine, capturing what needs your eyes, and keeping the calendar full without anyone stepping away from a client.</p>
  <div class="svc-grid">
    <div class="svc"><strong>Missed-call text-back</strong>A call you couldn't take mid-service becomes a text conversation in seconds, instead of a voicemail you clear at close.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Answers the menu questions</strong>Services, rough timings, what's included, gift cards, parking, whether you take walk-ins — answered instantly and accurately, any hour.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Never quotes a custom service</strong>Colour, extensions and corrections get captured — length, current colour, what they're after — then handed to you. It only quotes what you've published.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Fills cancellations</strong>When a slot opens, it offers it out and takes the first yes, so a late cancellation doesn't become a dead two hours.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Keeps people rebooking</strong>A nudge when a client is due, so the six-week colour cycle doesn't quietly stretch to ten and the monthly massage doesn't lapse.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Human handoff</strong>Anything needing your judgment — a correction, a complaint, an unusual request — comes to you with a summary of the conversation.</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="inner-sec" style="padding-top: 10px;">
  <div class="sec-eyebrow">Who it's built for</div>
  <h2>Wherever the service outlasts the phone call</h2>
  <p class="lede">Booth renters, small teams and full spas all hit the same wall: the person best placed to answer is the person mid-service.</p>
  <div class="svc-grid">
    <div class="svc"><strong>Hair salons</strong>Long colour services and a phone that rings hardest exactly when the whole floor is booked solid.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Booth renters &amp; solo stylists</strong>You are the stylist, the receptionist and the marketing department. The phone always loses to the client in your chair.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Massage therapists</strong>Ninety minutes with a phone that has to be silent. Every enquiry lands in a queue you work between clients.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Day spas</strong>Multi-service bookings, packages and gift cards mean more questions per enquiry than any other appointment business.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Nail &amp; lash studios</strong>Short services, high volume, and constant questions about fills, timing and aftercare.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Multi-chair teams</strong>Enquiries captured with the service and stylist preference, so the right person picks them up instead of everything landing in one pile.</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="inner-sec" style="padding-top: 10px;">
