<section class="inner-sec" style="padding-top: 10px;">
  <div class="proof-band">
    <div class="sec-eyebrow">Where the line is</div>
    <h2>It never prices what it can't see</h2>
    <p>Anything on your published menu, it can answer all day. Anything that depends on the person in front of you — how much colour is already on their hair, whether that correction is a three-hour job or a three-visit one — gets captured and handed to you. Guessing there costs more than a missed call ever will.</p>
    <div class="proof-points">
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>Published prices only</strong>
        <span>Menu services get real answers. Custom work gets the variables captured and a straight "your stylist will confirm" — never a number you didn't set.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>No advice on the work</strong>
        <span>Whether a colour will lift, whether extensions suit them, whether a massage will help a specific complaint — flagged for a human, never guessed at.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>Your policies, word for word</strong>
        <span>Deposits, late arrivals, cancellation windows and no-show rules repeated exactly as you've written them, so nobody is quoted a policy you don't have.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>Saturday morning, same coverage</strong>
        <span>It doesn't get flustered when every chair is full and the phone hasn't stopped. The twentieth caller gets the same answer as the first.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

